From 9ca35cd5a7e5856728cea22801ceea9631565ce3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 12:47:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replace scripted REPL with a real local-model chat backed by
 Ollama

The old claude-repl.ts matched keywords against canned strings and was not
imported anywhere. Removed it rather than leaving a simulation next to the
real thing.

- server/routes/ollama.js: status + streaming chat proxy. Streams NDJSON
  straight through so tokens appear as generated, and aborts the upstream
  generation when the client disconnects.
- app/src/lib/ollama.ts: client with incremental NDJSON parsing.
- app/src/components/terminal/AiChat.tsx: chat panel with model picker,
  fenced-code rendering, and a Stop that really stops.
- Terminal.tsx: the Bot button now switches a session between shell and model.
- server/test-ollama.mjs: harness covering streaming and every error path.

Proxying through our own backend avoids Ollama's CORS restrictions and keeps
working when the editor is opened from another machine on the network.
